Civgraph Elections: the go-public change set (prepared 11 Nov 2026; NOT APPLIED).

Apply only with the owner's approval in chat. From the repository root:

    git apply --check docs/tasks/elections-go-public.patch    # dry run: says whether it applies
    git apply docs/tasks/elections-go-public.patch            # make the change
    (if main has moved and it no longer applies cleanly: git apply -3 docs/tasks/elections-go-public.patch)

What it changes (the whole switch; nothing else is needed for the page itself):

  site/apps/elections/index.html   noindex meta removed; canonical https://civgraph.net/elections/ and the
                                   site's share card (Open Graph and Twitter tags, the standard 1200x630 image)
  site/apps/elections/app.js       each view's canonical and og:url are its own path (the query is tool state)
  site/_headers                    X-Robots-Tag noindex dropped for /elections and /elections/*; kept for
                                   /apps/elections/* (the same page at its file address, the widget, the files)
  site/_redirects                  comment only
  site/apps/index.html             the Apps page card
  site/index.html                  the home page's Apps panel links it ("Four focused tools")
  scripts/build/build-sitemap.mjs  /elections/ in TOP_LEVEL_PAGES
  site/sitemaps/pages.xml          the same, as the builder writes it
  data/database/r2-publication-allowlist.json      the data/elections-app/ prefix, reviewed (rationale,
                                   evidence, rights), in the same change as the upload as the allowlist requires
  packages/api/src/handlers/_public-prefixes.js    regenerated from it (node scripts/build/public-prefixes.mjs)
  scripts/build/build-site-partials.mjs            comment only
  tests                            the "not public" assertions become "public" ones: share-meta lists the page,
                                   elections-app-lib, elections-app-prep (prefix allowlisted) and the browser spec
                                   (indexable, canonical, linked from /apps/ and the home page)

The main header's nav is unchanged: the app sits under Apps, like Words in parliament. Embedding stays off
(frame-ancestors 'self' on /apps/elections/embed/*); allowing it is a separate one-line decision in site/_headers.

After applying: the R2 upload (scripts/publish/elections-app-r2-upload.mjs --upload), the rebuild that
re-stamps cache tokens (npm run build), the checks, then the usual publish. The exact steps are in the
stream's LANDING.md (D:\civgraph-intake\launch-2026-11-11\landing\elections-prep.md).

